(7240735, 1121742, 38921, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by LN13:</b></div><hr/><i> I really wish the side of the ripple hadn''t been chopped off.  This photo begs for a landscape crop, rather than square. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I agree with you 100%.  Unfortunately I had the flashes too close to the water and they created some harsh and ugly reflections on the edge of the ripple that needed to be cropped out.</td>', 'Originally posted by LN13: I really wish the side of the ripple hadn''t been chopped off.  This photo begs for a landscape crop, rather than square.   I agree with you 100%.  Unfortunately I had the flashes too close to the water and they created some harsh and ugly reflections on the edge of the ripple that needed to be cropped out.', '2014-07-14 10:15:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(7240736, 1121742, 38921, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Ja-9:</b></div><hr/><i> Can you explain what your set up was for the pan???  I''m not sure if that''s what I''m seeing or not...I think it''s a pan with saran wrap around it???<br/> <br/>I really had this pegged for one of the top 3...excellent execution.  I just wish I had lighting that I could play with... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The pan is just a paint pan for a roller.  It was filled to the rim with water, no saran wrap.</td>', 'Originally posted by Ja-9: Can you explain what your set up was for the pan???  I''m not sure if that''s what I''m seeing or not...I think it''s a pan with saran wrap around it??? I really had this pegged for one of the top 3...excellent execution.  I just wish I had lighting that I could play with...   The pan is just a paint pan for a roller.  It was filled to the rim with water, no saran wrap.', '2014-07-14 10:16:28.000000', NULL, 0),
